# Split second doesn't stop triggered abilities (CR 702.61b, the ruling): casting Krosan Grip, a noncreature spell, triggers
# Bot1's Harmonic Prodigy's prowess, which goes on the stack above Grip and resolves first (+1/+1 until end of turn). Grip
# then destroys Bot2's Oblivion Ring, an enchantment (CR 701.8), and the Ring's leaves-the-battlefield ability returns the
# Mox Ruby it had exiled (CR 603.6c, 610.3).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Harmonic Prodigy
Krosan Grip
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Black Lotus
Oblivion Ring
Island x15

